# RFP Workflow

This workspace contains prompt-based skills for transforming raw RFP input into
PRDs, task breakdowns, and Gherkin stories.

Default mode: run the **full workflow** skill once and let it execute the chain.
The skill opens with a **Planning summary** (planning-style kickoff),
then runs the pipeline and pauses only at human checkpoints (clarifications, PRD,
decomposition, export).

## Workflow order
rfp-normalize-rfp -> rfp-clarification-pass -> rfp-draft-prd -> [rfp-refine-prd] -> rfp-task-breakdown -> rfp-user-stories -> rfp-sync-trackers

## One-shot execution (recommended)
Use @.agent/skills/rfp-full-workflow/skill.md with your input RFP.
The full workflow skill emits a **Planning summary** first, then pauses only at human checkpoints (clarifications, infographic model, PRD,
decomposition, export).

## Fixed rules
- Hierarchy is always: Epic -> Feature -> Story -> Task. Never deviate.
- Clarification pass ALWAYS runs. It is non-blocking. Produce assumptions if answers are absent.
- Every artifact must include `## Assumptions` and `## Open Questions` sections.
- Outputs go to the `outputs/` directory.
- Use templates from the `templates/` directory.

## How to invoke a skill
Open the skill file (e.g. `.agent/skills/rfp-draft-prd/skill.md`) then press Cmd+L and
say: "Run this skill with the following input: [paste text]"

Or in chat, reference the skill file directly:
"Use @.agent/skills/rfp-draft-prd/skill.md and apply it to: [paste text]"

## Export targets
- Google Sheets: task-breakdown CSV block via Sheets MCP or manual import.
- GitHub Projects: stories as issues via GitHub MCP or JSON import.
- Jira: stories as issues via Jira MCP or CSV import.
